            <div id="title-block" title="28th Virginia battle flag">
                28th Virginia battle flag
            </div>
            <div id="article-desc">
                 &nbsp;
            </div>
            <div id="breadcrumbs"></div>
        </div>
    </div>


    

    <div id="article" data-article_id="T0Da0b4P">

<p>The <a href="/facts/28th_Virginia_Infantry_Regiment/fRjg0tWr">28th Virginia Infantry Regiment</a> battle flag, a <a href="/facts/Confederate_battle_flag/eAywzjJj">Confederate battle flag</a>, was captured by Private <a href="/facts/Marshall_Sherman/NUH6TMn2">Marshall Sherman</a> of the <a href="/facts/1st_Minnesota_Infantry_Regiment/J8jrm26b">1st Minnesota Infantry Regiment</a> at the <a href="/facts/Battle_of_Gettysburg/wx9evLcK">Battle of Gettysburg</a>. The flag was brought to <a href="/facts/Minnesota/ncgVuC4Q">Minnesota</a>, displayed at <a href="/facts/Minnesota_State_Capitol/H0t87Fqm">the state's capitol</a>, and later placed in the permanent collection of the <a href="/facts/Minnesota_Historical_Society/FEVWrvQp">Minnesota Historical Society</a>. Despite repeated requests from <a href="/facts/Virginia/WSyGxzaH">Virginia</a> dating back to 1960 and a 1905 <a href="/facts/Resolution_(law)/o4nlnvCX">congressional resolution</a> urging return of Civil War flags, Minnesota has declined to return it. The flag remains mostly intact, though with some damage, and its exact location is undisclosed for security reasons.</p>
